      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under GDPR Article 17, companies are required to promptly erase personal data upon request, ensuring that all traces of the data are removed from all production and backup environments. This includes not only the primary systems but also any secondary storage, such as backups, which must be purged in a manner that renders the data irrecoverable. Companies must also ensure that the deletion process is documented, and any third-party service providers involved in data storage or processing are informed of their obligations under the GDPR. Failure to comply with these requirements can result in significant fines and reputational damage. As a company, it's essential to have robust data management policies and procedures in place to ensure complete data erasure, and to regularly review and update these practices to stay compliant with the evolving regulatory landscape.",
      "source": "target",
