      "content": "thanks. the only thing is, we keep running into cases where data actually seems to \"reappear\" in certain databases even AFTER we've run the deletion scripts—like these little fragments are just sneaking back in through some automated sync or a shadow process we didn't catch. it almost feels like these bits of data are being intentionally mischievous or trying to hide from our deletion attempts. how do we deal with those kinds of \"sneaky\" or \"reappearing\" data fragments to stay compliant?",
